# ~/.localgroups - app groups for this machine
#
# This file is READ, not sourced: no `export` needed, and it is never
# committed. script/install and bin/dot-doctor read it; $DOTFILES_GROUPS
# overrides it for a single run (and in CI).
#
# Copy this file to ~/.localgroups and uncomment what this machine wants:
#
#   cp system/localgroups.example ~/.localgroups
#
# Each line: group names, space- or comma-separated. All uncommented lines
# combine, so work plus personal is valid. Available groups are the
# Brewfile.<name> files in the repo root. With no active line (or no file
# at all) only the shared Brewfile is installed.
#
# Create this BEFORE the first `script/bootstrap` so the shared apps and
# the group's apps install in one pass; adding it later means running
# `dot` once more.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored.

# work
# personal
